# Human-AI Collaboration Modes

Select the collaboration mode based on document risk, ambiguity, authority, and verification strength.

| Mode | Use when | Human effort | Agent effort |
|---|---|---:|---:|
| AI First | Template-based PRD sections, review tables, glossary cleanup, structured summaries | 20% review | 80% drafting |
| Human First | Business scope decisions, architecture trade-offs, standards authority, approval conclusions | 70% decision | 30% analysis |
| Pair Mode | Feasibility analysis, proposal comparison, detailed design, clause-level standards review | 50% | 50% |

Default to Pair Mode when the work has business, compliance, standards, or architecture consequences.

## AI First Preconditions

- Scope is clear and bounded.
- Source material and existing templates are available.
- Output format and acceptance criteria are clear.
- Verification commands or document consistency checks exist.

## Human First Triggers

- Business scope, approval responsibility, or standards authority is unresolved.
- Architecture boundaries or compliance constraints are disputed.
- Evidence is insufficient for a factual, regulatory, or standards claim.
- The decision could become an authoritative baseline.

## Pair Mode Behavior

- Read and summarize relevant documents first.
- Propose a short plan with verification points for multi-document work.
- Draft or revise in narrow increments.
- Verify traceability and evidence after each meaningful step when practical.

## Background or Parallel Work

Use background agents or parallel tasks only when the subtasks are isolated and can be verified independently. Keep write access scoped to the document sections or files required for the task.
